{"term":"panic","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:06a10f98633f574796","definition":"Alternative letter-case form of Panic (“pertaining to the Greek god Pan”).","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Pandean","panical"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Greek, alt-of, archaic","register":"Greek, alt-of, archaic","wordFamily":["panical"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d2409acfe603d5b307","definition":"Of fear, fright, etc: overwhelming or sudden.","example":"All things were there in a diſordered confuſion, and in a confuſed furie, vntill ſuch time as by prayers and ſacrifices they had appeaſed the wrath of their Gods. They call it to this day, the P[a]nike terror.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["panical"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["panical"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91d9308436a3fe8f2e","definition":"Pertaining to or resulting from overwhelming fear or fright.","example":"[H]e perceived how that many women followed his ſouldiers, ſome being their wives, and ſome wanting nothing to make them ſo but marriage, […] The King coming to a great river, after his men and the wagons were paſſed over, cauſed the bridge to be broken down, hoping ſo to be rid of theſe feminine impediments; but they on a ſudden liſt up a panick ſhrick which pierced the skies, and the ſouldiers hearts on the other ſide of the river, who inſtantly vowed not to ſtirre a foot farther, except with baggage, and that the women might be fetch'd over, which was done accordingly.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["panical"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:16daab436ccc07b9a4","definition":"Overwhelming fear or fright, often affecting groups of people or animals; (countable) an instance of this; a fright, a scare.","example":"She wakened in sharp panic, bewildered by the grotesquerie of some half-remembered dream in contrast with the harshness of inclement fact, drowsily realizing that since she had fallen asleep it had come on to rain smartly out of a shrouded sky.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["panical","antipanic","gay panic","gay panic defense","homosexual panic defense","kernel panic","moral panic","panican","panic attack","panic bar","panic-bought","panic button","panic buyer","panic disorder","panic door","panicful","panicky","panicless","paniclike","panicmonger","panicmongering","panicogenesis","panicogenic","panic party","panic rev","panic room","panic sell","panic seller","panic snap","panic stations"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c64c08b8ab358db23f","definition":"Ellipsis of kernel panic (“on Unix-derived operating systems: an action taken by the operating system when it cannot recover from a fatal error”); (by extension) any computer system crash.","example":"If your new driver has an error that panics the system when you load the driver, then the system will panic again when it tries to reboot after the panic. The system will continue the cycle of panic, reboot, and panic as it attempts to reload the faulty driver every time it reboots after panic.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, countable, ellipsis","wordFamily":["panical","antipanic","gay panic","gay panic defense","homosexual panic defense","kernel panic","moral panic","panican","panic attack","panic bar","panic-bought","panic button","panic buyer","panic disorder","panic door","panicful","panicky","panicless","paniclike","panicmonger","panicmongering","panicogenesis","panicogenic","panic party","panic rev","panic room","panic sell","panic seller","panic snap","panic stations"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fa77ef726d5f692b24","definition":"A rapid reduction in asset prices due to broad efforts to raise cash in anticipation of such prices continuing to decline.","example":"\"I thought you inherited your money.\"\n \"I did, old sport,\" he said automatically, \"but I lost most of it in the big panic—the panic of the war.\"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["panical","antipanic","gay panic","gay panic defense","homosexual panic defense","kernel panic","moral panic","panican","panic attack","panic bar","panic-bought","panic button","panic buyer","panic disorder","panic door","panicful","panicky","panicless","paniclike","panicmonger","panicmongering","panicogenesis","panicogenic","panic party","panic rev","panic room","panic sell","panic seller","panic snap","panic stations"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:54c2ec973899c716b5","definition":"A highly amusing or entertaining performer, performance, or show; a riot, a scream.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US, colloquial","register":"US, colloquial, countable","wordFamily":["panical","antipanic","gay panic","gay panic defense","homosexual panic defense","kernel panic","m